cover/ — keyboard cover touchpad (backlog, not installed by "install.sh all")

Problem (SM-W627, 2026-11-10): when the keyboard cover is connected to the
running tablet, its keyboard works but its touchpad sends nothing. After a cold
boot, or after one sleep/wake cycle of the tablet (s2idle), the touchpad works.

Tried without effect: re-sending the touchpad feature reports (input mode,
surface switch, latency; also as an off/on change), re-binding the driver, a
USB reset, a 0.3 s USB runtime suspend/resume of the cover (remote wakeup on).

gbook-touchpad-wake (+ .service, 90-gbook-cover.rules) is the last attempt:
USB runtime suspend/resume of the cover, USB reset as fallback. Install with
"install.sh cover" only for further experiments.

Workaround: press the power button (sleep), press it again (wake).
